836.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-01T19:18:32+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Ayush Pandey</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134621143,imgsize-96406.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[New liquor shops in Bengal must maintain 500-metre gap from schools, religious places]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/new-liquor-shops-in-bengal-must-maintain-500-metre-gap-from-schools-religious-places/articleshow/134618267.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134618267.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[In a bid to regulate the liquor trade, the West Bengal government has raised the distance criteria for new liquor outlets from educational institutions and places of worship. Urban areas will now need to maintain a 500-meter distance, while rural areas must ensure a full kilometer. Existing outlets remain unaffected by these changes, which also grant provisions for relocating under specific circumstances.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/new-liquor-shops-in-bengal-must-maintain-500-metre-gap-from-schools-religious-places/articleshow/134618267.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/new-liquor-shops-in-bengal-must-maintain-500-metre-gap-from-schools-religious-places/articleshow/134618267.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-01T18:28:25+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Mahima Sharma</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134619055,imgsize-75462.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Evening news wrap: UAE orders probe into flydubai incident; India enters men's hockey finals at the Asian Games &amp; more]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/evening-news-wrap-uae-orders-probe-into-flydubai-incident-india-enters-mens-hockey-finals-at-the-asian-games-more/articleshow/134618415.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134618415.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/evening-news-wrap-uae-orders-probe-into-flydubai-incident-india-enters-mens-hockey-finals-at-the-asian-games-more/articleshow/134618415.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/evening-news-wrap-uae-orders-probe-into-flydubai-incident-india-enters-mens-hockey-finals-at-the-asian-games-more/articleshow/134618415.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-01T18:13:33+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Pranjal Pandey</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134619532,imgsize-105660.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA['Show me one damaged vehicle': Nitin Gadkari's dare on ethanol blending, targets vested interests]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/show-me-one-damaged-vehicle-nitin-gadkaris-dare-on-ethanol-blending-targets-vested-interests/articleshow/134617029.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134617029.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[Union minister Nitin Gadkari highlighted the advantages of the ethanol-blending program during the Bihar Investor Summit 2026. He stated that millions of vehicles have been operating on ethanol-blended petrol since 2022 without significant complaints. Gadkari emphasized that farmers can benefit financially from diversifying into ethanol production from agricultural products. He urged investors to consider Bihar's potential in various sectors, including tourism and agriculture.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/show-me-one-damaged-vehicle-nitin-gadkaris-dare-on-ethanol-blending-targets-vested-interests/articleshow/134617029.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/show-me-one-damaged-vehicle-nitin-gadkaris-dare-on-ethanol-blending-targets-vested-interests/articleshow/134617029.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-01T17:13:52+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Trisha Mahajan</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134617819,imgsize-492217.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Himachal implements mandatory dress code for teachers in government CBSE schools]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/himachal-implements-mandatory-dress-code-for-teachers-in-government-cbse-schools/articleshow/134617151.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134617151.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[Himachal Pradesh has introduced a mandatory dress code for teachers in 148 government CBSE schools. The dress code aims to enhance professionalism and uniformity among educators while catering to local climatic conditions. Female teachers have multiple attire options, while male teachers have a single formal requirement. The state also plans to establish 100 new CBSE schools and has filled around 2,000 teaching posts.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/himachal-implements-mandatory-dress-code-for-teachers-in-government-cbse-schools/articleshow/134617151.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/himachal-implements-mandatory-dress-code-for-teachers-in-government-cbse-schools/articleshow/134617151.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-01T16:50:47+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Pranjal Pandey</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134617253,imgsize-95174.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Dipke vs Gyanesh Kumar: CJP to launch nationwide protest from October 2, demands CEC's resignation]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/dipke-vs-gyanesh-kumar-cjp-to-launch-nationwide-protest-from-october-2-demands-cecs-resignation/articleshow/134616983.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134616983.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/dipke-vs-gyanesh-kumar-cjp-to-launch-nationwide-protest-from-october-2-demands-cecs-resignation/articleshow/134616983.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/dipke-vs-gyanesh-kumar-cjp-to-launch-nationwide-protest-from-october-2-demands-cecs-resignation/articleshow/134616983.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-01T16:43:06+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Ayush Pandey</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134617066,imgsize-1175590.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Few responsibilities in a civilised society are as profound as that entrusted to a doctor, says SC, while cancelling Ramesh Mhatre’s bail]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/few-responsibilities-in-a-civilised-society-are-as-profound-as-that-entrusted-to-a-doctor-says-sc-while-cancelling-ramesh-mhatres-bail/articleshow/134616432.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134616432.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[In a significant move, the Supreme Court of India has revoked the bail of Ramesh Mhatre, a 73-year-old municipal corporator, following his arrest for allegedly attacking medical professionals. Initially granted bail in July, Mhatre's case was revisited owing to reservations expressed by the High Court regarding the broader implications for democracy.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/few-responsibilities-in-a-civilised-society-are-as-profound-as-that-entrusted-to-a-doctor-says-sc-while-cancelling-ramesh-mhatres-bail/articleshow/134616432.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/few-responsibilities-in-a-civilised-society-are-as-profound-as-that-entrusted-to-a-doctor-says-sc-while-cancelling-ramesh-mhatres-bail/articleshow/134616432.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-01T16:30:53+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Swati Deshpande</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134616642,imgsize-68174.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Amrinder Singh Raja Warring changes X bio after stepping down as Punjab Congress chief]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/amrinder-singh-raja-warring-quits-as-punjab-congress-chief-amid-factional-feud-changes-x-bio/articleshow/134614893.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134614893.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/amrinder-singh-raja-warring-quits-as-punjab-congress-chief-amid-factional-feud-changes-x-bio/articleshow/134614893.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/amrinder-singh-raja-warring-quits-as-punjab-congress-chief-amid-factional-feud-changes-x-bio/articleshow/134614893.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-01T15:33:37+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Rohitashwa Ranjan</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134615001,imgsize-99692.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Police were helpless, people feared mafia before 2017: UP CM Yogi]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/police-were-helpless-people-feared-mafia-before-2017-up-cm-yogi/articleshow/134614978.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134614978.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[Uttar Pradesh Chief Minister Yogi Adityanath spoke about the state's challenges and police issues before 2017. He emphasized the progress made since then, including police reforms and technology integration. The Chief Minister also shared plans for improved traffic initiatives with interceptor vehicles. Meanwhile, Congress president Ajay Rai criticized the government's response to recent rain damage in Gorakhpur. He demanded compensation for affected residents and accountability from officials for their actions.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/police-were-helpless-people-feared-mafia-before-2017-up-cm-yogi/articleshow/134614978.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/police-were-helpless-people-feared-mafia-before-2017-up-cm-yogi/articleshow/134614978.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-01T15:33:03+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Mahima Sharma</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134615020,imgsize-78333.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA['Indomitable bravery’: Indian flydubai pilot Smit Machchhar to be awarded ‘Visisht Gujarat Garima Award’]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/indomitable-bravery-indian-flydubai-pilot-smit-machchhar-to-be-awarded-visisht-gujarat-garima-award/articleshow/134613847.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134613847.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[Captain Smit Machchhar was injured by his co-pilot who planned to crash their aircraft. Despite being attacked, Machhar managed to save the lives of 174 passengers. The courageous actions of Machhar have garnered attention and respect globally. Gujarat Chief Minister Bhupendra Patel announced the award to honor Machhar's bravery. The pilot is currently recovering from his injuries and is receiving well-wishes from across the nation.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/indomitable-bravery-indian-flydubai-pilot-smit-machchhar-to-be-awarded-visisht-gujarat-garima-award/articleshow/134613847.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/indomitable-bravery-indian-flydubai-pilot-smit-machchhar-to-be-awarded-visisht-gujarat-garima-award/articleshow/134613847.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-01T14:53:14+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Trisha Mahajan</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134614280,imgsize-64788.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Watch: DYFI activists allegedly attack Kerala minister OJ Janeesh’s car in Kannur]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/watch-dyfi-activists-allegedly-attack-kerala-minister-oj-janeeshs-car-in-kannur/articleshow/134613716.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134613716.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/watch-dyfi-activists-allegedly-attack-kerala-minister-oj-janeeshs-car-in-kannur/articleshow/134613716.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/watch-dyfi-activists-allegedly-attack-kerala-minister-oj-janeeshs-car-in-kannur/articleshow/134613716.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-01T14:42:52+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Priyanka Jaiswal</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134613757,imgsize-